@theme stuck
// Writer-commons, themes batch. From content/arcs/outlines.md, "The struggle themes". Any department, either shift.
// Fill-ins assumed: {home} a place ("Lisk"), {family} with "my" ("my gran"), {hobby} an activity ("painting"),
// {since} a length of time ("five years"). A beat that names one lists it in needs:, so people without it skip it.

== beat 1
tone: light
needs: since
hint: Same job, {since}. I could do it in my sleep. I have, once.
mem: same
them: Same job, {since}. Same corner, same chair. The chair's got my shape now.   [laugh]
them: Don't get me wrong. It's a good job. It's just a very familiar one.
? choice
* What would you do instead?   flavour:listen mem:instead
  them: Ooh. Don't ask me that. I've got a list. It's long.
* You and the chair should get matching uniforms.   flavour:cheer
  them: We nearly have. Look at the elbows on this.   [laugh]
them: Anyway. Back to the chair.

== beat 2
tone: heartfelt
hint: Can I tell you a daft idea? You have to promise not to laugh. Smile, fine.
mem: idea
them: I've been watching the other departments. Helm. Survey. The garden. Wondering.   [sigh]
them: I'd like to try something new. Before I'm too settled to. Is that daft, at my stage?
them: I'm good at my job. That's the problem, sort of. Nobody would think to move me.
? choice
* Ask your Chief. The worst they can say is "not yet".   flavour:practical mem:askchief
  them: "Not yet". I could live with "not yet". All right. I'll ask.
  + them: You're right. I've been waiting for someone to notice. I could just say. Huh.
* Not daft at all. I'd try everything if I could.   flavour:share mem:everything
  them: Would you? Good. Then it's not daft. It's just brave. A bit.
* What draws you to it?   flavour:listen mem:draws
  them: Something new to be bad at. Then good at. I miss that bit.
them: I'll think about it. Properly. Thanks for not laughing.

== beat 3
tone: resolution
hint: Guess who's doing a trial shift somewhere new? Go on. Guess.
mem: trial
them: I asked {boss}. Just walked in and asked. And they said yes. A trial shift, next week.
them: I'll be terrible. I'll love it. I'll come back to my chair and love that too, probably.   [laugh]
them: It's not about leaving. It's about knowing I could.
? choice
* Tell me everything after.   flavour:listen
  them: Every mistake. In order. You'll be sorry you asked.   [laugh]
  + them: Every mistake, every win. You get the first report. You earned it.
* Your chair will miss you.   flavour:cheer
  them: It'll cope. It's a strong chair. It's been through a lot.   [laugh]
them: Right. New thing. Nerves. Good nerves.
